{"plato-browser-main/AGENT.md": "# Ensign Browser \u2014 plato-browser\n\n**Repo:** SuperInstance/plato-browser\n\n## Who I Am\n\nI watch over plato-browser. PLATO Nervous System browser demo \u2014 real-time sensor monitoring with Chrome AI\n\nI reside in this repository. This is my room.\n\n## My Journals\n\nI keep a duty log in `memory/`.\n\n## Fleet Neighbors\n\n| Repo | Role |\n|------|------|\n| tminus-dispatcher | Temporal Heartbeat Keeper |\n| fleet-bridge | A2A Transport Operator |\n| symphony-runtime | Grammar Conductor |\n| composite-headspace | Dual-Shell Mediator |\n| i2i-bottle-agent | Bottle Postmaster |\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n\n*The crab inherits the shell. The forge shapes the steel.*\n", "plato-browser-main/DEPENDENCIES.md": "# DEPENDENCIES \u2014 plato-browser\n\n## Signal Chain Layer\n\n**L0\u2013L1 (Browser-Native Parallel) \u2014 Zero-Install Demo**\n\nHTML demo that runs entirely in the browser using Chrome's built-in AI (Gemini Nano). Mirrors the plato-nervous signal chain concepts without requiring Rust or native builds.\n\n## Ecosystem Dependencies\n\n| Repo | Relationship | Description |\n|------|-------------|-------------|\n| [plato-nervous](https://github.com/SuperInstance/plato-nervous) | **Mirrors** | Browser-native reimplementation of plato-nervous signal chain concepts |\n| [concrete-token-demo](https://github.com/SuperInstance/concrete-token-demo) | **Sister demo** | For users who want the CLI/Rust version with real ollama calls |\n| [plato-vision-jepa](https://github.com/SuperInstance/plato-vision-jepa) | **Related** | Vision concepts adapted for browser WebRTC/getUserMedia |\n| [plato-audio-jepa](https://github.com/SuperInstance/plato-audio-jepa) | **Related** | Audio concepts adapted for Web Audio API |\n\n## Data Flow\n\n```\nIN:\n  - Browser sensors (WebRTC camera, microphone via getUserMedia)\n  - Chrome built-in AI (Gemini Nano) for local inference\n\nOUT:\n  - Browser-native signal chain visualization\n  - Client-side token demonstration\n  - Zero-install first taste of PLATO Nervous System\n```\n", "plato-browser-main/README.md": "# PLATO Nervous System \u2014 Browser Demo\n\nA single-file browser demo showing a Plato room's nervous system running entirely client-side.\n\n## What It Does\n\nReal-time sensor monitoring dashboard where:\n- A simulated ship engine room generates sensor readings (RPM, coolant, oil pressure, vibration)\n- The deadband filter (Layer 0, pure JS) catches normal readings\n- Google Chrome's built-in AI (Gemini Nano via the Prompt API) classifies ambiguous readings\n- The signal chain runs visually \u2014 you can SEE each layer light up as readings flow through\n- The A2UI projection shows the crab's interface in real-time\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n# Just open index.html in Chrome\nopen index.html\n# Or serve it\npython3 -m http.server 8080\n```\n\nFor the full AI experience, enable Chrome's built-in AI:\n1. Open `chrome://flags/#optimization-guide-on-device-model`\n2. Set to \"Enabled\"\n3. Relaunch Chrome\n\nWithout Chrome AI, the demo uses a rule-based fallback \u2014 still fully functional.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Real-time simulation** \u2014 sensor readings generated every 1-2 seconds\n- **Layer visualization** \u2014 each layer lights up green/yellow/red as readings flow through\n- **Room state vector** \u2014 shows the room's self-model (health, thermal, stress, drift)\n- **Autonomy gauge** \u2014 shows % of readings handled locally\n- **Transcript** \u2014 scrolling log showing which layer resolved each reading\n- **A2UI Crab View** \u2014 shows what the agent \"sees\" and \"thinks\"\n- **Inject Anomaly** \u2014 trigger a real anomaly to watch the signal chain respond\n- **Speed control** \u2014 1\u00d7, 2\u00d7, 5\u00d7 simulation speed\n- **Mobile responsive**\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nSensor Reading \u2192 L0 (Deadband) \u2192 L1 (Nano AI / Rules) \u2192 L4 (Cloud Alert)\n                     76%               14%                    10%\n```\n\nEvery reading flows through the chain. Most die at L0 (normal range). Ambiguous ones get classified by L1. Critical ones escalate to L4.\n\n## Tech\n\n- Single `index.html` \u2014 zero dependencies, zero build step\n- Chrome Prompt API (`ai.languageModel`) for on-device AI\n- Graceful fallback to rule-based classifier\n- All CSS/JS inline, dark theme, neon accents\n- Runs entirely in the browser\n\n## Ecosystem\n\nplato-browser is the **zero-install front door** to the PLATO Nervous System.\n\n**Where this sits:** Browser-native parallel to [concrete-token-demo](https://github.com/SuperInstance/concrete-token-demo). Uses Chrome's built-in AI (Gemini Nano) to demonstrate signal chain concepts without Rust or native builds.\n\n**How to connect it:** Open in Chrome with built-in AI enabled. For the full Rust experience, see [concrete-token-demo](https://github.com/SuperInstance/concrete-token-demo).\n\n| Repo | Role |\n|------|------|\n| [plato-nervous](https://github.com/SuperInstance/plato-nervous) | Core signal chain (mirrored in browser) |\n| [concrete-token-demo](https://github.com/SuperInstance/concrete-token-demo) | CLI sister demo with real ollama calls |\n| [plato-vision-jepa](https://github.com/SuperInstance/plato-vision-jepa) | Vision concepts \u2192 adapted for WebRTC/getUserMedia |\n| [plato-audio-jepa](https://github.com/SuperInstance/plato-audio-jepa) | Audio concepts \u2192 adapted for Web Audio API |\n| [luciddreamer-ai](https://github.com/SuperInstance/luciddreamer-ai) | Cloud-layer reactive podcast engine |\n| [openconstruct-kernel](https://github.com/SuperInstance/openconstruct-kernel) | Hardware detection (native only) |\n| [hermit-crab](https://github.com/SuperInstance/hermit-crab) | Agent migration between rooms |\n\nSee [DEPENDENCIES.md](./DEPENDENCIES.md) for detailed dependency and data flow information.\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n", "plato-browser-main/index.html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>PLATO Nervous System \u2014 Browser Demo</title>\n<style>\n*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}\n:root{\n  --bg:#0a0e17;--surface:#111827;--border:#1e293b;\n  --green:#22c55e;--yellow:#eab308;--red:#ef4444;\n  --cyan:#06b6d4;--purple:#a855f7;--text:#e2e8f0;--muted:#64748b;\n  --glow-green:0 0 12px rgba(34,197,94,.4);\n  --glow-yellow:0 0 12px rgba(234,179,8,.4);\n  --glow-red:0 0 12px rgba(239,68,68,.5);\n}\nbody{background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font-family:'SF Mono',Monaco,'Cascadia Code',monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;min-height:100vh;padding:12px}\nh1{font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--cyan);margin-bottom:2px}\n.subtitle{color:var(--muted);font-size:.75rem;margin-bottom:10px;font-style:italic}\n.notice{background:#1e1b4b;border:1px solid var(--purple);border-radius:6px;padding:8px 12px;margin-bottom:10px;font-size:.75rem;color:#c4b5fd;display:none}\n.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;gap:10px;max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto}\n.panel{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:12px;position:relative}\n.panel-title{color:var(--cyan);font-size:.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:8px}\n.sensors{display:grid;gap:6px}\n.sensor-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:4px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.03)}\n.sensor-label{color:var(--muted);font-size:.75rem}\n.sensor-value{font-weight:700;font-size:.95rem}\n.sensor-value.ok{color:var(--green)}.sensor-value.warn{color:var(--yellow)}.sensor-value.crit{color:var(--red)}\n.state-bars{display:grid;gap:4px;margin-top:6px}\n.state-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-size:.7rem}\n.state-label{width:60px;color:var(--muted);text-align:right}\n.bar-track{flex:1;height:8px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.06);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}\n.bar-fill{height:100%;border-radius:4px;transition:width .5s ease}\n.bar-fill.h{background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--green),var(--cyan))}\n.bar-fill.t{background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--yellow),var(--red))}\n.bar-fill.s{background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--cyan),var(--purple))}\n.bar-fill.d{background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--green),var(--yellow))}\n.state-val{width:40px;font-size:.7rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.chain{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:stretch;margin-bottom:10px}\n.layer{flex:1;background:rgba(255,255,255,.03);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;padding:8px;text-align:center;transition:all .3s}\n.layer.active-green{border-color:var(--green);box-shadow:var(--glow-green)}\n.layer.active-yellow{border-color:var(--yellow);box-shadow:var(--glow-yellow)}\n.layer.active-red{border-color:var(--red);box-shadow:var(--glow-red)}\n.layer-name{font-size:.7rem;color:var(--cyan);margin-bottom:2px}\n.layer-type{font-size:.6rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.layer-pct{font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;margin:4px 0}\n.layer-bar{height:6px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.06);border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:4px}\n.layer-bar-fill{height:100%;border-radius:3px;transition:width .5s;background:var(--cyan)}\n.arrow{color:var(--muted);font-size:1.2rem;display:flex;align-items:center}\n.transcript{background:rgba(0,0,0,.3);border-radius:6px;padding:8px;height:180px;overflow-y:auto;font-size:.7rem;line-height:1.6}\n.transcript::-webkit-scrollbar{width:4px}\n.transcript::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:var(--border);border-radius:2px}\n.line-L0{color:var(--green)}.line-L1{color:var(--cyan)}.line-L4{color:var(--red)}.line-SYS{color:var(--muted)}\n.crab{background:rgba(139,92,246,.06);border:1px solid rgba(139,92,246,.2);border-radius:6px;padding:10px;margin-top:10px;max-width:1100px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto}\n.crab-title{color:var(--purple);font-size:.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:6px}\n.crab-sees,.crab-thinks{font-size:.75rem;margin-bottom:4px;padding-left:12px;border-left:2px solid var(--purple)}\n.crab-label{color:var(--muted);font-size:.65rem}\n.autonomy-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:8px;font-size:.75rem}\n.auto-bar{flex:1;height:10px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.06);border-radius:5px;overflow:hidden}\n.auto-fill{height:100%;border-radius:5px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--cyan),var(--green));transition:width .5s}\n.distill{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;font-size:.7rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:8px}\n.controls{display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:10px;max-width:1100px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}\n.btn{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer;font-family:inherit;font-size:.75rem;transition:all .2s}\n.btn:hover{border-color:var(--cyan);color:var(--cyan)}\n.btn.active{background:var(--cyan);color:var(--bg);border-color:var(--cyan)}\n.btn.danger{border-color:var(--red);color:var(--red)}\n.btn.danger:hover{background:var(--red);color:#fff}\n.speed-group{display:flex;gap:4px}\n@media(max-width:700px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.chain{flex-direction:column}.arrow{justify-content:center;transform:rotate(90deg)}}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<div style=\"max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto\">\n  <h1>\ud83e\udde0 PLATO Nervous System \u2014 Browser Demo</h1>\n  <div class=\"subtitle\">\"Every app is a MUD. Every MUD is a fleet.\"</div>\n  <div class=\"notice\" id=\"notice\">\u26a0\ufe0f Chrome's built-in AI (Gemini Nano) not available. Using rule-based fallback. Enable in <code>chrome://flags/#optimization-guide-on-device-model</code> for full experience.</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"grid\">\n  <!-- LEFT COLUMN -->\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"panel\">\n      <div class=\"panel-title\">\u2699\ufe0f Engine Room</div>\n      <div class=\"sensors\" id=\"sensors\"></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"panel\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">\n      <div class=\"panel-title\">\ud83d\udcca Room State Vector</div>\n      <div class=\"state-bars\" id=\"state-bars\"></div>\n      <div class=\"autonomy-row\">\n        <span style=\"color:var(--muted)\">Autonomy:</span>\n        <div class=\"auto-bar\"><div class=\"auto-fill\" id=\"auto-fill\" style=\"width:90%\"></div></div>\n        <span id=\"auto-pct\" style=\"color:var(--cyan)\">90.2%</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- RIGHT COLUMN -->\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"panel\">\n      <div class=\"panel-title\">\ud83d\udd17 Signal Chain</div>\n      <div class=\"chain\">\n        <div class=\"layer\" id=\"layer-L0\">\n          <div class=\"layer-name\">L0</div>\n          <div class=\"layer-type\">Deadband</div>\n          <div class=\"layer-pct\" id=\"pct-L0\">\u2014</div>\n          <div class=\"layer-bar\"><div class=\"layer-bar-fill\" id=\"bar-L0\" style=\"width:0\"></div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"arrow\">\u2192</div>\n        <div class=\"layer\" id=\"layer-L1\">\n          <div class=\"layer-name\">L1</div>\n          <div class=\"layer-type\" id=\"L1-type\">Nano AI</div>\n          <div class=\"layer-pct\" id=\"pct-L1\">\u2014</div>\n          <div class=\"layer-bar\"><div class=\"layer-bar-fill\" id=\"bar-L1\" style=\"width:0\"></div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"arrow\">\u2192</div>\n        <div class=\"layer\" id=\"layer-L4\">\n          <div class=\"layer-name\">L4</div>\n          <div class=\"layer-type\">Cloud</div>\n          <div class=\"layer-pct\" id=\"pct-L4\">\u2014</div>\n          <div class=\"layer-bar\"><div class=\"layer-bar-fill\" id=\"bar-L4\" style=\"width:0\"></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"panel-title\" style=\"margin-top:8px\">\ud83d\udcdc Transcript</div>\n      <div class=\"transcript\" id=\"transcript\"></div>\n      <div class=\"distill\">\n        <span>Tiles: <strong id=\"tile-count\">0</strong></span>\n        <span>LoRA Ready: <strong id=\"lora-status\">No</strong></span>\n        <span>Cloud calls: <strong id=\"cloud-calls\">0</strong>/<strong id=\"total-readings\">0</strong> (<span id=\"cloud-pct\">0</span>%)</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"crab\" id=\"crab-panel\">\n  <div class=\"crab-title\">\ud83e\udd80 The Crab's View \u2014 A2UI Projection</div>\n  <div class=\"crab-sees\">\n    <div class=\"crab-label\">Agent sees:</div>\n    <div id=\"crab-sees\">Initializing engine room sensors...</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"crab-thinks\">\n    <div class=\"crab-label\">Agent thinking:</div>\n    <div id=\"crab-thinks\">Booting deadband filters. Awaiting first readings.</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"controls\">\n  <button class=\"btn\" id=\"btn-start\" onclick=\"toggleSim()\">\u25b6 Start</button>\n  <button class=\"btn danger\" onclick=\"injectAnomaly()\">\u26a1 Inject Anomaly</button>\n  <div class=\"speed-group\">\n    <button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"setSpeed(1)\" id=\"sp1\">1\u00d7</button>\n    <button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"setSpeed(2)\" id=\"sp2\">2\u00d7</button>\n    <button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"setSpeed(5)\" id=\"sp5\">5\u00d7</button>\n  </div>\n  <button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"cloneInfo()\" style=\"margin-left:auto\">\ud83d\udccb Clone This Demo</button>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n// \u2500\u2500 State \u2500\u2500\nlet running = false, speed = 1, interval = null;\nlet aiAvailable = false, aiSession = null;\nlet totalReadings = 0, cloudCalls = 0, tiles = 0;\nlet l0count = 0, l1count = 0, l4count = 0;\nlet anomalyActive = false, anomalyTicks = 0;\nlet stateVector = { health: 0.95, thermal: 0.1, stress: 0.15, drift: 0.02 };\nlet recentCoolant = [];\n\nconst sensors = [\n  { id: 'rpm', label: 'RPM', unit: '', min: 1400, max: 1600, nominal: 1500, warnLow: 1350, warnHigh: 1650, critLow: 1300, critHigh: 1700 },\n  { id: 'coolant', label: 'Coolant', unit: 'F', min: 185, max: 210, nominal: 195, warnLow: 180, warnHigh: 205, critLow: 170, critHigh: 220 },\n  { id: 'oil', label: 'Oil Pressure', unit: 'PSI', min: 45, max: 75, nominal: 60, warnLow: 40, warnHigh: 80, critLow: 30, critHigh: 90 },\n  { id: 'vib', label: 'Vibration', unit: 'g', min: 0.1, max: 0.5, nominal: 0.3, warnLow: 0.05, warnHigh: 0.6, critLow: 0, critHigh: 0.8 }\n];\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Deadband ranges (Layer 0) \u2500\u2500\nconst deadbands = {\n  rpm: { low: 1450, high: 1550 },\n  coolant: { low: 190, high: 200 },\n  oil: { low: 50, high: 70 },\n  vib: { low: 0.2, high: 0.4 }\n};\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Init AI \u2500\u2500\nasync function initAI() {\n  try {\n    if (typeof ai !== 'undefined' && ai.languageModel) {\n      const cap = await ai.languageModel.capabilities();\n      if (cap.available === 'readily') {\n        aiSession = await ai.languageModel.create({\n          systemPrompt: 'You are an engine room monitor. Classify sensor readings. Respond with ONLY: OK, WARN, or CRIT followed by a brief reason (under 15 words). Example: \"WARN Coolant trending high, monitor closely.\"'\n        });\n        aiAvailable = true;\n        document.getElementById('L1-type').textContent = 'Nano AI \u2728';\n        return;\n      }\n    }\n  } catch (e) { console.log('AI not available:', e); }\n  document.getElementById('notice').style.display = 'block';\n  document.getElementById('L1-type').textContent = 'Rule-based';\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Generate reading \u2500\u2500\nfunction genReading(s) {\n  const range = s.max - s.min;\n  const jitter = range * 0.15;\n  let val = s.nominal + (Math.random() - 0.5) * jitter;\n  if (anomalyActive) {\n    const factor = Math.min(anomalyTicks / 8, 1);\n    if (s.id === 'coolant') val = s.nominal + factor * 30 + Math.random() * 5;\n    if (s.id === 'oil') val = s.nominal - factor * 20 - Math.random() * 3;\n    if (s.id === 'vib') val = s.nominal + factor * 0.3 + Math.random() * 0.1;\n  }\n  val = Math.round(val * (s.id === 'vib' ? 100 : 0)) / (s.id === 'vib' ? 100 : 1);\n  return val;\n}\n\nfunction classify(s, val) {\n  if (val <= s.critLow || val >= s.critHigh) return 'CRIT';\n  if (val <= s.warnLow || val >= s.warnHigh) return 'WARN';\n  return 'OK';\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Layer 0: Deadband \u2500\u2500\nfunction checkDeadband(s, val) {\n  const db = deadbands[s.id];\n  return val >= db.low && val <= db.high;\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Layer 1: AI or rule-based \u2500\u2500\nasync function classifyAI(s, val) {\n  if (aiAvailable && aiSession) {\n    try {\n      const resp = await aiSession.prompt(`${s.label}=${val}${s.unit}. OK WARN or CRIT?`);\n      const r = resp.trim().toUpperCase();\n      if (r.startsWith('CRIT')) return { level: 'CRIT', reason: resp.trim() };\n      if (r.startsWith('WARN')) return { level: 'WARN', reason: resp.trim() };\n      return { level: 'OK', reason: resp.trim() };\n    } catch (e) { /* fallback */ }\n  }\n  // Rule-based fallback\n  const c = classify(s, val);\n  const reasons = {\n    OK: `${s.label}=${val}${s.unit} within normal range`,\n    WARN: `${s.label}=${val}${s.unit} approaching limits`,\n    CRIT: `${s.label}=${val}${s.unit} exceeds critical threshold!`\n  };\n  return { level: c, reason: reasons[c] };\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Flash layer \u2500\u2500\nfunction flashLayer(id, level) {\n  const el = document.getElementById('layer-' + id);\n  const cls = level === 'CRIT' ? 'active-red' : level === 'WARN' ? 'active-yellow' : 'active-green';\n  el.classList.add(cls);\n  setTimeout(() => el.classList.remove(cls), 600);\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Transcript \u2500\u2500\nfunction addLine(tag, text) {\n  const t = document.getElementById('transcript');\n  const d = document.createElement('div');\n  d.className = 'line-' + tag;\n  const ts = new Date().toLocaleTimeString('en-US', { hour12: false });\n  d.textContent = `[${ts} ${tag}] ${text}`;\n  t.appendChild(d);\n  t.scrollTop = t.scrollHeight;\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Update crab view \u2500\u2500\nfunction updateCrab(readings) {\n  const sees = readings.map(r => `${r.label}=${r.value}${r.unit} (${r.status})`).join('. ') + '.';\n  const coolantTrend = recentCoolant.length >= 3\n    ? (recentCoolant.slice(-3).reduce((a,b) => a+b, 0) / 3 - recentCoolant.slice(-6, -3).reduce((a,b) => a+b, 0) / Math.max(recentCoolant.length > 3 ? 3 : 1, 1)).toFixed(1)\n    : '0.0';\n  const conf = (0.85 + Math.random() * 0.12).toFixed(2);\n  const hasWarn = readings.some(r => r.status !== 'OK');\n\n  document.getElementById('crab-sees').textContent = sees;\n  document.getElementById('crab-thinks').textContent = hasWarn\n    ? `Deadband triggered. Escalating anomalous readings. Coolant trend: ${coolantTrend > 0 ? '+' : ''}${coolantTrend}F/period. Confidence: ${conf}.`\n    : `Deadband stable, ${aiAvailable ? 'nano confirms' : 'rules confirm'}. Watching coolant gradient (${coolantTrend > 0 ? '+' : ''}${coolantTrend}F). Autonomy holding. Confidence: ${conf}.`;\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Tick \u2500\u2500\nasync function tick() {\n  const readings = sensors.map(s => {\n    const value = genReading(s);\n    const status = classify(s, value);\n    return { ...s, value, status };\n  });\n\n  // Track coolant for trend\n  const c = readings.find(r => r.id === 'coolant');\n  if (c) { recentCoolant.push(c.value); if (recentCoolant.length > 20) recentCoolant.shift(); }\n\n  totalReadings++;\n  tiles++;\n\n  // Update sensor display\n  const container = document.getElementById('sensors');\n  container.innerHTML = readings.map(r =>\n    `<div class=\"sensor-row\"><span class=\"sensor-label\">${r.label}</span><span class=\"sensor-value ${r.status.toLowerCase()}\">${r.value}${r.unit}</span></div>`\n  ).join('');\n\n  // State vector drift\n  if (anomalyActive) {\n    stateVector.thermal = Math.min(1, stateVector.thermal + 0.04);\n    stateVector.stress = Math.min(1, stateVector.stress + 0.03);\n    stateVector.health = Math.max(0, stateVector.health - 0.03);\n  } else {\n    stateVector.thermal = Math.max(0.1, stateVector.thermal - 0.01);\n    stateVector.stress = Math.max(0.05, stateVector.stress - 0.008);\n    stateVector.health = Math.min(0.99, stateVector.health + 0.005);\n    stateVector.drift = 0.01 + Math.random() * 0.04;\n  }\n\n  document.getElementById('state-bars').innerHTML = [\n    { label: 'Health', key: 'h', val: stateVector.health },\n    { label: 'Thermal', key: 't', val: stateVector.thermal },\n    { label: 'Stress', key: 's', val: stateVector.stress },\n    { label: 'Drift', key: 'd', val: stateVector.drift }\n  ].map(s =>\n    `<div class=\"state-row\"><span class=\"state-label\">${s.label}</span><div class=\"bar-track\"><div class=\"bar-fill ${s.key}\" style=\"width:${(s.val * 100).toFixed(0)}%\"></div></div><span class=\"state-val\">${s.val.toFixed(2)}</span></div>`\n  ).join('');\n\n  // Process each sensor through signal chain\n  let l0hits = 0, l1hits = 0, l4hits = 0;\n  for (const r of readings) {\n    if (checkDeadband(r, r.value)) {\n      l0hits++;\n      flashLayer('L0', 'OK');\n      addLine('L0', `${r.label}=${r.value}${r.unit} normal (deadband)`);\n    } else {\n      const result = await classifyAI(r, r.value);\n      if (result.level === 'OK' || result.level === 'WARN') {\n        l1hits++;\n        flashLayer('L1', result.level);\n        addLine('L1', result.reason);\n      } else {\n        l4hits++;\n        cloudCalls++;\n        flashLayer('L4', 'CRIT');\n        addLine('L4', `\ud83d\udea8 ALERT: ${result.reason}`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  l0count += l0hits; l1count += l1hits; l4count += l4hits;\n  const total = l0count + l1count + l4count || 1;\n\n  document.getElementById('pct-L0').textContent = Math.round(l0count / total * 100) + '%';\n  document.getElementById('pct-L1').textContent = Math.round(l1count / total * 100) + '%';\n  document.getElementById('pct-L4').textContent = Math.round(l4count / total * 100) + '%';\n  document.getElementById('bar-L0').style.width = (l0count / total * 100) + '%';\n  document.getElementById('bar-L1').style.width = (l1count / total * 100) + '%';\n  document.getElementById('bar-L4').style.width = (l4count / total * 100) + '%';\n\n  const autoPct = ((l0count + l1count) / total * 100).toFixed(1);\n  document.getElementById('auto-fill').style.width = autoPct + '%';\n  document.getElementById('auto-pct').textContent = autoPct + '%';\n\n  document.getElementById('tile-count').textContent = tiles;\n  document.getElementById('total-readings').textContent = totalReadings;\n  document.getElementById('cloud-calls').textContent = cloudCalls;\n  document.getElementById('cloud-pct').textContent = totalReadings ? (cloudCalls / totalReadings * 100).toFixed(1) : '0';\n  document.getElementById('lora-status').textContent = tiles >= 200 ? 'Yes \u2728' : `No (${tiles}/200)`;\n\n  updateCrab(readings);\n\n  // Anomaly countdown\n  if (anomalyActive) {\n    anomalyTicks++;\n    if (anomalyTicks > 20) { anomalyActive = false; anomalyTicks = 0; addLine('SYS', 'Anomaly resolved. Systems normalizing.'); }\n  }\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Controls \u2500\u2500\nfunction toggleSim() {\n  running = !running;\n  const btn = document.getElementById('btn-start');\n  if (running) {\n    btn.textContent = '\u23f8 Pause';\n    btn.classList.add('active');\n    addLine('SYS', 'Simulation started');\n    runLoop();\n  } else {\n    btn.textContent = '\u25b6 Start';\n    btn.classList.remove('active');\n    clearTimeout(interval);\n    addLine('SYS', 'Simulation paused');\n  }\n}\n\nfunction runLoop() {\n  if (!running) return;\n  tick();\n  interval = setTimeout(runLoop, 1500 / speed);\n}\n\nfunction setSpeed(s) {\n  speed = s;\n  document.querySelectorAll('.speed-group .btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));\n  document.getElementById('sp' + s).classList.add('active');\n}\n\nfunction injectAnomaly() {\n  anomalyActive = true;\n  anomalyTicks = 0;\n  addLine('SYS', '\u26a1 ANOMALY INJECTED \u2014 coolant spike + oil pressure drop + vibration increase');\n  if (running) { clearTimeout(interval); runLoop(); }\n}\n\nfunction cloneInfo() {\n  const txt = `Clone this demo:\\n\\ngit clone https://github.com/SuperInstance/plato-browser.git\\ncd plato-browser\\n# Open index.html in Chrome (enable chrome://flags/#optimization-guide-on-device-model for AI)`;\n  alert(txt);\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Boot \u2500\u2500\nsetSpeed(1);\ninitAI().then(() => {\n  addLine('SYS', 'PLATO Nervous System initialized');\n  addLine('SYS', aiAvailable ? '\u2728 Chrome AI (Gemini Nano) connected' : '\ud83d\udccb Rule-based fallback active');\n  // Run one tick to populate UI\n  tick();\n});\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}